## What changed (GitHub writes, Dean-authorized 2026-07-29)

Reviewer replies to ev-shindin's round-1 COMMENTED reviews on C #1480 and D #1481 are now
**POSTED** (were held/unposted). Each reply points the reviewer at the specific commits that
addressed each point:

- **PR C #1480** — [issuecomment-5123171764](https://github.com/llm-d/llm-d-workload-variant-autoscaler/pull/1480#issuecomment-5123171764).
  Point 1 (no-EPP/arrival=0 → scale-down): intentional + safe (zero demand only *permits*
  scale-down; all-live-agree gate governs); in-code reasoning documented in `94accd09`; operator
  hard-requirement tracked by expanding #1498 (see below). Point 2 (broken-query vs idle):
  RequestRate is a completion rate not arrival, so the instantaneous cross-check would
  false-positive on ramp-down — documented in `94accd09`; the sound temporal signal ships as the
  observability-only WARN in D `c32235be`.
- **PR D #1481** — [issuecomment-5123171907](https://github.com/llm-d/llm-d-workload-variant-autoscaler/pull/1481#issuecomment-5123171907).
  Point 1 (duplicated sentinels): fixed in `61060530` (exported `pipeline.ReasonNoData`/`ReasonError`).
  Point 2 (`lastGoodAnalysis` eviction): fixed in `c32235be` (selective per-cycle prune of departed
  models). `AnalyzedAt` aside acknowledged (contract noted in liveness comments `33226cd4`/`c32235be`).

- **Issue #1498** body expanded from two to **three** operator-doc requirements — added:
  "The ThroughputAnalyzer must not be enabled without EPP arrival metrics present" (busy model
  reads as idle → spurious scale-down). Raised by the C #1480 review. Title unchanged. Doc change
  itself still lands as a PR against llm-d/llm-d (out of WVA-repo scope; #1498 is the tracker).

